    50	18
    51	This story rests on filings in Beatty v. Trump and D.C. Preservation League v. Trump; the court's May 29 opinions; the board's August meeting record; the August 28 joint report; the September 16 scheduling order; federal statutes governing the Kennedy Center; the September 17 minute order as reproduced by two admitted carriers; and five coverage records checked against those documents.
    52	The request and the ruling
    53	The judge refused the hearing and added an advance-notice rule
    54	Beatty asked for an emergency hearing after the main building closed and after the board voted to close it for renovation. The defendants answered that the immediate closure was separate from the renovation decision, while Floca described it as a temporary safety measure. Executive Director Matt Floca declared that structural deterioration created acute risks to public safety and that the initial closure would last seven days unless extended.
