    67	Minute order, as reproduced by UPI
    68	To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events, the Court hereby ORDERS Defendants [the Kennedy Center board] to provide such notice in writing to Plaintiffs in both cases more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court in D.C. Preservation League [a separate case], including but not limited to any 'demolition' of the Center's main building.
    69	21
    70	The order also required the administration to update Cooper by September 23 on the status of the temporary closure and emergency repairs. Beatty's counsel said Cooper also ordered discovery into the board's actions related to a potential demolition.
