    74	The period is more than 30 days.
    75	The operative sentence says notice must arrive more than 30 days before implementation. “30 days” is a useful shorthand, but it drops the word that sets the boundary.
    76	21
    77	The order follows the plans already put before the court.
    78	It does not say “any major physical changes” require notice. That phrase comes from the AP headline. The trigger in the reproduced order is a change to the scope of the project plans presented in the preservation case, with demolition named as an example.
    79	20
    80	21
