stance, the REACH Expansion and the addition to the Center’s parking garage—would have required Congress’s permission because they added new structures to the campus. As for the seemingly less intrusive addition of a “photovoltaic system” on the roof of the main building, see 20 U.S.C. § 76m, the Kennedy Center had to go to Congress anyway to secure a specific appropriation for the work, see id. § 76r(d), and it is not entirely clear from the statute itself whether express Congressional authorization was otherwise required. 23 
