data/sources/kennedy-center/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17.html:519:<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WASHINGTON, D.C., September 17, 2026 </strong>— Today, Judge Christopher R. Cooper <a href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72069932/beatty-v-trump/?filed_after=&amp;filed_before=&amp;entry_gte=&amp;entry_lte=&amp;order_by=desc">issued a ruling</a> in the ongoing Kennedy Center case that effectively prevents Donald Trump from demolishing the Kennedy Center without notice. Under Judge Cooper’s order, should the Board undertake “any changes to the scope of the project plans [&#8230;] including but not limited to any ‘demolition’ of the Center’s main building,” they must provide 30 days’ advance warning. Judge Cooper additionally ordered discovery into the Board’s actions related to a potential demolition and required the Board to update the Court by September 23 regarding the latest efforts to shutter the Center.</p>
