3-Judge orders Trump to give 30-day notice before any demolition of Kennedy Center
4-WASHINGTON − A federal judge effectively blocked President Donald Trump from taking immediate action to demolish the Kennedy Center, ordering on Sept. 17 that the center provide a 30-day notice to plaintiffs before any demolition or other major changes to the center's main building can begin.
5:It means the legality of any attempt to demolish the Kennedy Center ‒ which Trump has argued is necessary without substantial renovations ‒ would likely be subject to the judge's review during the 30-day period.
6-U.S. District Court Judge Christopher Cooper ordered the 30-day notice as he denied a request from Rep. Joyce Beatty ‒ the plaintiff suing Trump over the center ‒ for an emergency hearing. Beatty, a Democratic congresswoman from Ohio who serves on the board, is seeking the court's intervention to block the Kennedy Center board's vote this week to close the center for renovations.
7-Instead, the judge ordered the Trump-aligned Kennedy Center to submit a sworn declaration from a knowledgeable representative of the center who can attest to the emergency repairs that necessitated the closure. Justice Department attorneys argued in a court filing Sept. 17 that the closure is "temporary" to address emergency repairs, not to begin a two-year renovation project Trump has pushed.
--
9-But Trump wants recognition in return for his financial support. Trump has warned that he won't pursue renovations to the Kennedy Center unless a separate decision from Cooper this week keeping Trump's name off the center's building is overturned on appeal.
10-Cooper ruled the Kennedy Center's plan to add an inscription below the center's sign that says "renovated and restored by Donald J. Trump" cannot move forward. The judge said the inscription violates his previous order in May to remove Trump's name from the center's title and signage and violates the 1964 law that created the center to honor President Kennedy after his assassination.
11:Without renovations, Trump told reporters on Sept. 16 that the Kennedy Center will "end up being ripped down" because of its dilapidated state. The same day, Trump was pictured through a window on Air Force One reading a poster that says, "Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED."
