the Performing Arts.” 20 U.S.C. § 76j(a)(2)(F).

        Each of these statutes draw a distinction between the building—designated by Congress as

the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts—and the site or grounds, which is unnamed.

The Board’s jurisdiction therefore encompasses a complex of buildings, gardens, and landscape

features, each of which are maintained and administered by the Board. Indeed, in addition to the

“John F. Kennedy Memorial Center for the Performing Arts” building, the campus includes the

REACH Welcome Pavilion, the REACH Skylight Pavilion, and the REACH River Pavilion. 5 It

also includes the REACH Gardens, the Presidential Grove, and the Video Wall Lawn. 6 And there

is the REACH Plaza, North Plaza, River Plaza, Entrance Plaza, Victura Deck, and myriad

sculptures. 7


