The decisive gap is now confirmed in primary records. An August 24 Justice Department filing itself said the building could be “required to be taken down” and replaced by an amphitheater, while the page presents the demolition concern mainly through later remarks and a cropped placard. The September 18 attachments also contain substantial new closure, safety, cost, and board-ratification claims that the page reduces to a procedural note.
